WEBVTT


00:02:00.144 --> 00:02:01.183
Empty your mind.


00:02:02.021 --> 00:02:04.059
No distraction.
No emotion.


00:02:04.730 --> 00:02:06.853
Only calm and clarity.


00:02:17.362 --> 00:02:19.401
The Yoroi Bitsu.


00:02:20.406 --> 00:02:22.444
Our most sacred chest.


00:02:25.659 --> 00:02:28.824
The only remaining object
of the last Koga Ninja.


00:02:30.411 --> 00:02:32.449
It is the only final
resting place for the


00:02:32.578 --> 00:02:35.496
weapons of ninja warriors
through the ages.


00:02:36.956 --> 00:02:38.995
The powers they
hold are legendary.


00:02:39.958 --> 00:02:41.996
Each piece with it's own story,


00:02:43.586 --> 00:02:45.208
handed down from
generation to generation...


00:02:45.502 --> 00:02:47.541
for a thousand years.


00:02:48.838 --> 00:02:51.244
They were created for
one purpose only.


00:02:52.465 --> 00:02:54.919
Sudden and violent death.


00:03:04.096 --> 00:03:07.177
With these weapons,
the ninja became...


00:03:07.598 --> 00:03:08.796
much more than
a mere warrior.


00:03:10.099 --> 00:03:13.099
He become the most supreme
of the lethal dissidence


00:03:13.601 --> 00:03:15.640
and used them for profit
and wars.


00:03:19.813 --> 00:03:22.931
It became an art as
pure, as it was ruthless.


00:03:27.066 --> 00:03:29.106
Over the years...


00:03:29.610 --> 00:03:32.690
the Ninja forged,
the deadliest poisons,


00:03:33.737 --> 00:03:35.776
with only one antidote...


00:03:36.154 --> 00:03:38.193
they held the power of life,


00:03:39.157 --> 00:03:41.195
and death.


00:03:56.249 --> 00:03:58.288
Tradition says...


00:03:58.376 --> 00:04:00.947
that the Shinobu Katana Sword
has the power to take life.


00:04:02.127 --> 00:04:04.498
But in the hands of
a true Koga ninja.


00:04:05.420 --> 00:04:08.421
He has the power
to restore a life's spirit.


00:04:18.177 --> 00:04:22.054
The Yoroi Bitsu, and and it's secrets
were pushed from the battlefield,


00:04:22.118 --> 00:04:23.634
into the imagination


00:04:25.140 --> 00:04:27.179
but hidden from sight...


00:04:27.349 --> 00:04:29.388
safe in this ancient school,


00:04:29.475 --> 00:04:31.467
A single Yoroi Bitsu survived


00:04:32.601 --> 00:04:34.641
and the secret of
the ninja lived on...


00:04:35.229 --> 00:04:37.267
transforming the
disciplines of death...


00:04:37.688 --> 00:04:40.937
into Budo... a martial
art of enlightenment.


00:04:59.784 --> 00:05:01.822
- Masazuka.
- Yes!


00:05:11.248 --> 00:05:13.287
- Casey!
- Yes!


00:06:26.248 --> 00:06:28.285
Casey-san. Water?


00:06:29.999 --> 00:06:32.074
Thanks, Kiko.


00:06:36.211 --> 00:06:39.163
You are always working so late
more than anyone else.


00:06:40.963 --> 00:06:43.001
I guess I'm not so
good at sitting still.


00:06:45.925 --> 00:06:48.496
And not so good
at bo arts, neither.


00:07:03.476 --> 00:07:05.514
Well your father seems
to think I have potential.


00:07:07.769 --> 00:07:09.808
So does someone else.


00:07:12.355 --> 00:07:14.395
You know, we don't have
time for such things in the Dojo.


00:07:16.107 --> 00:07:18.146
No. We don't.


00:07:29.405 --> 00:07:32.592
I better get back.


00:08:16.389 --> 00:08:19.924
It must have been
very painful, for you.


00:08:24.061 --> 00:08:26.099
- It was in the past.
- The past...


00:08:27.188 --> 00:08:29.227
Defines a man...


00:08:29.313 --> 00:08:31.850
Tradition, heritage...


00:08:33.441 --> 00:08:35.479
Your parents.


00:08:37.986 --> 00:08:40.023
What's your point?


00:08:40.861 --> 00:08:42.900
We have traditions.
What do you have?


00:08:45.280 --> 00:08:47.320
A letter and a
photo from a mother,


00:08:47.990 --> 00:08:50.314
who abandoned
her only child.


00:08:51.242 --> 00:08:53.280
a memory of a drunk father,


00:08:53.451 --> 00:08:55.491
who killed himself.


00:08:59.497 --> 00:09:01.572
Masazuka!


00:09:42.354 --> 00:09:44.428
- Casey!
- Yes!


00:09:47.106 --> 00:09:49.144
- Masazuka!
- Yes.


00:11:25.034 --> 00:11:27.109
Masazuka!


00:11:45.169 --> 00:11:47.208
Sensei.


00:11:55.967 --> 00:11:58.006
Sensei.


00:12:57.584 --> 00:12:59.622
Sensei!


00:13:01.544 --> 00:13:03.583
Sensei!


00:13:41.066 --> 00:13:44.315
Welcome... brothers.


00:13:47.652 --> 00:13:50.273
Tonight, we come together...


00:13:51.696 --> 00:13:53.985
for another initiation ceremony.


00:13:55.448 --> 00:13:59.147
As our ranks and power
continue to grow.


00:14:00.867 --> 00:14:02.907
Throughout time society...


00:14:03.286 --> 00:14:06.784
has searched for guidance
from select groups of people.


00:14:07.663 --> 00:14:09.701
Leaders, we call them.


00:14:09.955 --> 00:14:12.032
Men of vision and action.


00:14:18.460 --> 00:14:20.998
Do you willingly
accept the bond?


00:14:47.663 --> 00:14:50.433
This historic agreement, lays
a foundation for a pipeline


00:14:51.437 --> 00:14:53.843
that will reach all the
way to the Bering Strait.


00:14:55.439 --> 00:14:57.477
Experts who believe,
that the merger of these


00:14:57.815 --> 00:15:00.483
two Russian companies
will create sufficient capital


00:15:00.692 --> 00:15:02.731
to win the bid
for the project.


00:15:03.027 --> 00:15:06.228
Mr Klimitov will make a statement,
once the contract has been signed.


00:16:38.077 --> 00:16:40.116
Please. Whatever you want


00:16:40.538 --> 00:16:42.577
I'll give it.


00:16:47.666 --> 00:16:50.239
Ladies and gentlemen of the press,
thank you for your patience.


00:16:51.461 --> 00:16:53.784
In a few minutes will get a
statement from, Mr Klimitov.


00:16:54.462 --> 00:16:56.501
Thank you.


00:17:08.970 --> 00:17:11.376
- Tell me some good news.
- Keep watching.


00:17:12.221 --> 00:17:14.628
Mr. Klimitov should be exiting
the theatre any moment now.


00:17:15.182 --> 00:17:17.422
We should have a
statement, for you shortly.


00:17:18.184 --> 00:17:20.221
Wait a minute! Wait a minute!
Something...


00:17:22.894 --> 00:17:24.968
He's bleeding, what appears
to be from his neck.


00:17:26.729 --> 00:17:29.136
Chaos. There's total
chaos here at Vladivostok.


00:17:29.897 --> 00:17:31.771
Yuri Klimitov,
a Russian oil mogul,


00:17:32.065 --> 00:17:34.103
appears to be injured.


00:17:35.275 --> 00:17:37.813
As promised, no more merger.


00:17:39.277 --> 00:17:41.316
- Cheers, gentlemen.
- Yes, cheers!


00:17:59.622 --> 00:18:02.537
Greetings friends and honoured
guests from abroad.


00:18:03.582 --> 00:18:06.560
It is a day... we recognise


00:18:06.585 --> 00:18:09.202
by displaying a highest honour,


00:18:10.003 --> 00:18:12.077
a sacred treasure...


00:18:12.462 --> 00:18:14.502
of our ninja ancestry...


00:18:15.381 --> 00:18:17.419
The Yoroi Bitsu.


00:18:17.673 --> 00:18:19.712
After 30 years as Soke,


00:18:21.175 --> 00:18:23.547
I must now, name a successor.


00:20:02.814 --> 00:20:04.888
The Yoroi Bitsu must be taken


00:20:05.190 --> 00:20:07.229
to the other side of the world.


00:20:07.400 --> 00:20:09.474
To be guarded.
Hidden from sight.


00:20:10.234 --> 00:20:13.067
There is a man, a scholar,
the only person I trust,


00:20:13.360 --> 00:20:15.400
to keep it's power
from falling into


00:20:15.863 --> 00:20:17.901
the hands of Masazuka.


00:20:30.537 --> 00:20:32.575
Sensei.


00:21:14.394 --> 00:21:16.433
Namiko,


00:21:49.539 --> 00:21:51.577
You see, the Dean is
a close personal friend.


00:21:52.248 --> 00:21:54.287
Considering the safety we need,


00:21:54.499 --> 00:21:56.870
I thought it wise to store
it in the university vault.


00:21:57.877 --> 00:21:59.914
This way.


00:22:59.701 --> 00:23:01.739
So tell me, Casey,


00:23:01.868 --> 00:23:03.908
How does a young
man like yourself...


00:23:03.996 --> 00:23:06.366
- end up in a Japanese Dojo?
- You mean a white guy?


00:23:07.580 --> 00:23:10.248
Well you don't exactly
fit the demographic profile.


00:23:13.376 --> 00:23:15.414
Well, okay.


00:23:16.543 --> 00:23:18.581
My father was a marine.


00:23:18.669 --> 00:23:20.661
He was stationed in Okinawa,


00:23:20.796 --> 00:23:22.835
so me and my mother,
moved there with him.


00:23:23.130 --> 00:23:25.169
But they didn't get along to well.


00:23:25.382 --> 00:23:27.420
She ended up leaving.


00:23:28.257 --> 00:23:30.297
The problem was...


00:23:30.385 --> 00:23:33.253
- She didn't take me with her.
- Oh, I'm sorry to hear that.


00:23:33.719 --> 00:23:35.758
You see, my dad, uh...


00:23:37.262 --> 00:23:39.302
He was a drunk.


00:23:39.598 --> 00:23:41.636
I guess she couldn't take it any more,


00:23:41.890 --> 00:23:44.345
He finally drank himself of the end
of a cliff in a car, when I was twelve..


00:23:46.976 --> 00:23:49.597
So anyway a friend of the
family took me to see Sensei


00:23:49.854 --> 00:23:51.892
rather than let them
ship me off to an orphanage


00:23:53.438 --> 00:23:55.477
and... that's
where I stayed.


00:23:56.398 --> 00:23:58.437
I haven't looked back since.


00:26:15.223 --> 00:26:17.261
Masazuka.


00:29:39.542 --> 00:29:42.245
I remember the day I met
Takada Sensei in Japan.


00:29:43.587 --> 00:29:45.625
His technical skills were amazing.


00:30:09.016 --> 00:30:11.056
Well I hope we
can just close the deal.


00:30:12.186 --> 00:30:14.260
Press is already here.
I'll get back to you.


00:30:14.353 --> 00:30:17.139
Mr. Temple, what is your reaction
to the pipeline murders in Russia?


00:30:17.604 --> 00:30:19.644
It's a tragedy.


00:30:19.773 --> 00:30:21.812
Isn't it true that Temple Oil shares
are up by 20 percent since,


00:30:21.899 --> 00:30:23.890
that deal fell through?


00:30:24.025 --> 00:30:26.063
So is the stock market.


00:30:26.359 --> 00:30:28.397
Is there a correlation to that to?


00:30:28.568 --> 00:30:30.608
But they were your competitors...


00:30:30.862 --> 00:30:33.987
These were well respected men and
their deaths are a threat to all of us.


00:30:34.739 --> 00:30:37.489
I'm willing to pledge
10 million dollars...


00:30:38.491 --> 00:30:40.530
to anyone who can
bring in these killers.


00:30:41.034 --> 00:30:43.072
What about the police
sources who say this is another


00:30:43.285 --> 00:30:46.237
In a chain of killings involving
an organization called "The Ring".


00:30:48.330 --> 00:30:50.736
I can't comment on something
I'm not familiar with.


00:30:51.373 --> 00:30:53.412
Isn't it true, your company
has benefited each time.


00:30:53.958 --> 00:30:55.995
I'm sorry. I gotta take this.


00:30:58.586 --> 00:31:01.371
A friend? Didn't expect
to hear from you.


00:31:02.504 --> 00:31:04.542
Always a pleasure
doing business with you.


00:31:05.589 --> 00:31:10.163
Now, I must ask you
to do a job for me.


00:31:12.343 --> 00:31:15.654
Namiko, did you
try your father again?


00:31:16.345 --> 00:31:18.383
Still no answer.


00:31:18.679 --> 00:31:20.718
He should be there.


00:31:21.013 --> 00:31:24.511
I... Don't understand.


00:31:57.283 --> 00:31:59.322
- You looking for Rebecca?
- Yes.


00:32:00.910 --> 00:32:02.950
Are you her friend?


00:32:03.204 --> 00:32:05.242
Sort of, she, uh...


00:32:05.538 --> 00:32:07.577
She knew my parents.


00:32:10.248 --> 00:32:12.288
She had a stroke.


00:32:12.542 --> 00:32:14.367
She past away a few months ago.


00:32:14.584 --> 00:32:15.912
I'm sorry.


00:32:29.509 --> 00:32:31.548
Ah, Casey. Good to see you back.


00:32:32.761 --> 00:32:34.836
Afraid, I'm just
on my way to bed.


00:32:35.888 --> 00:32:38.637
Namiko's is still up.
I'll see you in the morning.


00:32:39.014 --> 00:32:41.090
- Okay. Good night, Professor.
- Good night.


00:32:50.313 --> 00:32:52.351
Did you find her?


00:32:57.983 --> 00:33:00.022
I guess she's been
sick for a while.


00:33:21.496 --> 00:33:23.533
Who's there?


00:33:25.456 --> 00:33:27.532
Get down!


00:34:15.275 --> 00:34:17.729
You know why I'm here.
Where's the box?


00:34:52.461 --> 00:34:54.500
Are you okay?


00:35:03.801 --> 00:35:05.840
Come on.


00:35:15.765 --> 00:35:17.805
Go!


00:37:29.881 --> 00:37:31.919
We need a room.


00:37:39.718 --> 00:37:41.757
- Time's up!
- Give me five more minutes!


00:37:48.182 --> 00:37:50.220
What?


00:37:53.475 --> 00:37:55.551
Please.


00:37:59.854 --> 00:38:01.893
Let's get you warm.


00:38:11.403 --> 00:38:13.974
Rui... Akira...


00:38:15.906 --> 00:38:17.943
- Professor.
- I know, I know.


00:38:20.074 --> 00:38:22.148
You heard what they wanted.


00:38:22.491 --> 00:38:24.531
- Masazuka.
- Yeah.


00:38:27.995 --> 00:38:30.034
If he knows where we are...


00:38:30.371 --> 00:38:32.409
That means my father...


00:38:33.415 --> 00:38:35.536
No, no. We don't
know that yet.


00:38:37.458 --> 00:38:39.497
Listen to me. We
don't know that yet.


00:38:50.715 --> 00:38:52.755
The victim is Dr Paul Garrison,


00:38:52.842 --> 00:38:54.833
He was a professor, author,


00:38:55.009 --> 00:38:57.499
lecturer, specialist
on the far east.


00:38:57.928 --> 00:38:59.966
We got any suspects?


00:39:00.137 --> 00:39:02.213
Oh, yeah.


00:39:03.181 --> 00:39:05.137
One, Namiko Takeda...


00:39:05.473 --> 00:39:07.512
and Casey Bowman.


00:39:11.436 --> 00:39:13.473
Still no answer.


00:39:15.354 --> 00:39:17.392
We just keep trying.


00:39:20.649 --> 00:39:22.687
Although we no
official confirmation...


00:39:22.858 --> 00:39:25.608
sources tell us, it was
a gang-land style hit.


00:39:26.047 --> 00:39:27.609
Witnesses claim


00:39:27.610 --> 00:39:29.964
there were several victims,
including the professor.


00:39:30.237 --> 00:39:32.275
Can we go to the police?


00:39:32.363 --> 00:39:33.596
Police are searching for two suspects,


00:39:33.597 --> 00:39:35.027
who were seen fleeing the scene.


00:39:35.115 --> 00:39:38.507
A male
Caucasian, a female Asian


00:39:38.807 --> 00:39:40.076
reportedly in their mid-twenties,


00:39:40.451 --> 00:39:42.489
and are considered armed
and extremely dangerous.


00:39:44.203 --> 00:39:46.277
We have to tell
them about, Masazuka.


00:39:46.370 --> 00:39:48.446
He wasn't even there.


00:39:49.665 --> 00:39:51.702
And people are dead.
The police... no.


00:39:52.249 --> 00:39:54.287
They could hold on
to us, for a long time.


00:39:55.625 --> 00:39:58.412
You heard Garrison. The Dean
knows we put something in that safe.


00:39:59.502 --> 00:40:01.541
Pretty soon, somebody's
gonna make a connection.


00:40:02.504 --> 00:40:05.254
- So?
- We have to move the Yoroi Bitsu.


00:40:07.216 --> 00:40:09.337
Tomorrow.


00:40:11.634 --> 00:40:13.672
It's okay.


00:40:14.635 --> 00:40:16.675
We'll get through this.


00:40:30.519 --> 00:40:32.557
Namiko?


00:40:34.147 --> 00:40:36.186
Namiko?


00:40:43.652 --> 00:40:45.690
The girl I was with,
have you seen her?


00:40:48.112 --> 00:40:50.151
Two coffee's please
and two sandwiches.


00:40:50.239 --> 00:40:52.276
Okay.


00:41:11.459 --> 00:41:13.498
Hey, what are you doing?


00:41:13.918 --> 00:41:15.956
Getting us some food.


00:41:17.170 --> 00:41:19.208
- Sandwiches are coming up.
- Thank you.


00:41:27.841 --> 00:41:29.880
Let me get you some sugar.


00:41:51.938 --> 00:41:53.977
Down!


00:42:00.318 --> 00:42:02.357
Don't shoot us!


00:42:40.590 --> 00:42:43.458
- Come on!
- Remember. We need her alive.


00:43:01.642 --> 00:43:03.682
Subway!


00:43:13.817 --> 00:43:15.891
Subway.


00:43:27.240 --> 00:43:29.278
Hey, excuse me!


00:44:37.112 --> 00:44:39.149
Masazuka.


00:44:40.154 --> 00:44:42.230
They could be
working for him.


00:44:55.747 --> 00:44:57.821
Come on.


00:47:39.668 --> 00:47:41.706
Police! Hands up!


00:47:42.086 --> 00:47:44.125
Put your hands on your head!


00:47:53.802 --> 00:47:55.259
Masazuka.


00:47:55.552 --> 00:47:59.345
You have, what
I asked for, or not?


00:48:03.431 --> 00:48:05.470
Tell our colleague,
what happened.


00:48:05.891 --> 00:48:08.178
We found them, but
they didn't have the box.


00:48:08.266 --> 00:48:10.592
- Where are they?
- The police arrested them.


00:48:10.936 --> 00:48:12.973
I asked...


00:48:14.020 --> 00:48:16.059
Where?


00:48:16.980 --> 00:48:19.018
West 54 precinct.


00:48:19.272 --> 00:48:21.312
But there's no way
we can get to them.


00:48:35.699 --> 00:48:37.736
Pray I find them...


00:48:37.824 --> 00:48:39.817
Or your next.


00:48:50.790 --> 00:48:52.829
What are you doing in this country?


00:48:53.208 --> 00:48:55.246
I was visiting a friend.


00:48:55.333 --> 00:48:57.326
- The dead professor?
- Yes.


00:48:59.378 --> 00:49:01.417
Why'd you kill him?


00:49:01.504 --> 00:49:03.827
- I didn't.
- Then why'd you run?


00:49:04.213 --> 00:49:06.704
Because we had to.
Those men wanted to kill us!


00:49:08.591 --> 00:49:10.630
- Really?
- Hmm.


00:49:13.843 --> 00:49:15.883
You have no idea what
you're dealing with here.


00:49:21.557 --> 00:49:23.595
I'm all ears.


00:49:48.196 --> 00:49:50.235
Sir, can I help you?


00:49:50.530 --> 00:49:53.068
I'm here for, Namiko Takeda.
She was arrested earlier today.


00:49:53.825 --> 00:49:55.862
- I'm her attorney.
- Okay, send him in.


00:49:55.950 --> 00:49:57.989
I'll meet him
in my office.


00:50:03.371 --> 00:50:06.572
- Your lawyer just showed up.
- My lawyer?


00:50:24.673 --> 00:50:26.712
That's quite a story, Casey.


00:50:28.675 --> 00:50:30.714
So, your saying that
this Masazuka guy,


00:50:31.344 --> 00:50:33.382
who nobody's
seen or heard of.


00:50:33.511 --> 00:50:35.550
or who may have heard,
is on your trail


00:50:35.805 --> 00:50:37.842
is after you to...
retrieve a box?


00:50:38.430 --> 00:50:40.470
The Yoroi Bitsu.


00:50:40.808 --> 00:50:42.846
Right.


00:50:43.976 --> 00:50:46.014
So where is it?


00:50:46.811 --> 00:50:48.849
I can't tell you that.


00:50:52.355 --> 00:50:54.394
Why not?


00:51:06.654 --> 00:51:09.062
It's him. Masazuka, he's here.


00:51:10.157 --> 00:51:12.195
I'll send him your regards.


00:51:12.283 --> 00:51:15.364
Hey, don't leave me like this.
Hey!


00:51:18.453 --> 00:51:20.528
Hey, what's going on?


00:51:50.845 --> 00:51:52.883
Jesus Christ, lady. We're just
trying to get you out of here.


00:51:53.721 --> 00:51:55.761
God! Let's go.


00:51:58.849 --> 00:52:00.888
Let's go.


00:52:53.420 --> 00:52:55.459
Hey, hey lady!


00:55:10.412 --> 00:55:12.451
- On the ground!
- Where is she?


00:55:13.329 --> 00:55:15.368
I said get on the ground!


00:55:15.456 --> 00:55:17.447
What do you think
is happening here?


00:55:17.623 --> 00:55:19.663
Get down, or I'll
put you down.


00:55:49.475 --> 00:55:51.549
Some fairy tale, huh?


00:56:33.914 --> 00:56:36.321
- Just let her go.
- Not before I kill you.


00:57:55.293 --> 00:57:57.330
No!


01:01:10.565 --> 01:01:12.603
Where is she?


01:01:15.151 --> 01:01:17.189
Who did you call, your source?


01:01:17.485 --> 01:01:19.524
Nobody.


01:01:20.194 --> 01:01:22.768
- Who did you call?
- It's just a number to keep in contact!


01:01:23.531 --> 01:01:25.568
I don't know who's
on the other end!


01:01:26.114 --> 01:01:28.190
Wait! Wait!


01:01:28.366 --> 01:01:30.404
I'll tell you where you
can find him, okay?


01:01:31.868 --> 01:01:33.148
I'm listening.


01:01:46.501 --> 01:01:49.037
Welcome... brothers.


01:02:04.761 --> 01:02:07.925
We control the life and
blood of this planet.


01:02:08.720 --> 01:02:10.797
A dedicated "Ring of Brothers".


01:02:15.600 --> 01:02:17.638
Kill him!


01:02:35.110 --> 01:02:37.149
Come on, stop him!


01:05:33.790 --> 01:05:35.830
- Masazuka.
- Casey?


01:05:36.167 --> 01:05:38.205
Where is she?


01:05:40.628 --> 01:05:42.665
Very close.


01:05:45.256 --> 01:05:47.293
If you've hurt her,
I swear to God...


01:05:47.464 --> 01:05:49.503
Listen to me.


01:05:50.549 --> 01:05:52.588
I want the Yoroi Bitsu.


01:05:54.843 --> 01:05:56.882
Okay. You'll get it...


01:05:57.053 --> 01:05:59.092
for Namiko.


01:05:59.887 --> 01:06:02.639
Construction site of 49th
and church at 3am.


01:07:40.400 --> 01:07:42.438
How many more of you?


01:07:42.693 --> 01:07:44.732
Two.


01:07:46.945 --> 01:07:49.021
I'm sorry, guys.


01:07:50.364 --> 01:07:52.402
Freeze!


01:07:56.242 --> 01:07:58.317
Is that the box?


01:07:59.244 --> 01:08:01.282
You should believe me now.


01:08:01.953 --> 01:08:04.029
Let's take a ride down town.


01:08:04.456 --> 01:08:06.909
No. I'm gonna give
you what you want.


01:08:08.708 --> 01:08:10.745
You're gonna let me do,
what I have to do.


01:09:19.538 --> 01:09:22.201
Masazuka! Let her go!


01:09:23.331 --> 01:09:25.405
Not until I get the Yoroi Bitsu.


01:09:25.748 --> 01:09:27.788
Don't, Casey!


01:09:35.545 --> 01:09:37.585
It's all yours.


01:09:37.715 --> 01:09:39.752
Now, let her go.


01:10:12.399 --> 01:10:15.481
49th and church.
Masazuka and Casey.


01:10:15.860 --> 01:10:16.856
I want them both dead.


01:10:18.027 --> 01:10:20.066
What you have, is mine.


01:10:22.530 --> 01:10:24.569
So, come and get it.


01:11:42.156 --> 01:11:44.194
Go! Go!


01:13:31.257 --> 01:13:33.295
Get down!


01:14:16.615 --> 01:14:18.653
You need this,


01:14:18.741 --> 01:14:20.780
to keep her alive.


01:15:31.322 --> 01:15:33.360
No!


01:15:49.874 --> 01:15:51.912
Yes.


01:15:53.876 --> 01:15:55.914
Such anger.


01:16:04.631 --> 01:16:07.712
This the police,
drop your weapons.


01:16:08.134 --> 01:16:09.925
Put your hands in the air
and lay down on the ground.


01:16:22.558 --> 01:16:24.596
Again, drop your weapons.


01:16:24.934 --> 01:16:27.638
Put your hands in the air
and lay down on the ground.


01:17:41.351 --> 01:17:43.389
Namiko.


01:17:44.686 --> 01:17:46.724
Namiko.


01:17:50.686 --> 01:17:52.250
I'm sorry.


01:17:56.420 --> 01:17:58.505
I can't save you.


01:18:05.802 --> 01:18:07.574
I love you!


01:18:10.181 --> 01:18:12.266
I've always loved you.


01:18:19.564 --> 01:18:21.231
Tradition says...


01:18:22.170 --> 01:18:27.174
that the Shinobu Katana Sword
possesses both, the power to take life


01:18:27.800 --> 01:18:31.031
and also the life's spirit,
the power to heal.


01:18:33.488 --> 01:18:35.525
The power to heal.


01:18:57.098 --> 01:18:59.135
Namiko. Drink.


01:19:01.014 --> 01:19:03.049
Drink.


01:19:12.548 --> 01:19:14.584
Come back to me.


01:19:16.212 --> 01:19:18.249
Namiko.


01:21:22.801 --> 01:21:24.874
This is one hell of
a mess here, Casey.


01:21:25.591 --> 01:21:27.627
It's gonna take day's... hell,


01:21:27.840 --> 01:21:29.876
maybe even weeks
to clean this up.


01:21:30.005 --> 01:21:32.041
Not that it really
matters anymore, does it?


01:21:34.461 --> 01:21:36.496
The main thing is,
"The Ring's" broken.


01:21:36.709 --> 01:21:38.746
Temple's in custody.


01:21:39.082 --> 01:21:41.119
Then there's you two...


01:21:43.622 --> 01:21:45.694
Your late for your plane.


01:21:47.369 --> 01:21:49.938
Now get the hell out
of here, permanently.


